Z||000000||lowfunds||11-18-2000||08:51 AM||||I read a while back about terryk installing this setup. Did he or anyone else find out what axles will be needed for the swap? I thought it was said that only the right side axle might have to be longer, but I did not see anymore info on the subject. If anyone has done this swap or has anymore info on the subject please respond. thank you ||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowfunds||11-18-2000||11:54 AM||||Anyone??? I know there is a lot of 3800 conversions out there someone has to know. And with this swap does the stock ecm need to be retained in anyway? Info please||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-18-2000||12:26 PM||||search the word axle in both the tech and general forums. it's out there. I can't rememeber where. I think everyone's been doing the 60E I don't know if the 65 is the same.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||11-18-2000||12:57 PM||||I used 94+ A-car (Ciera/Century/6000 w/ 4T60E) axles with the manual trans Fiero outer CV's swapped on. The 92+ U-van (Trans Sport, Lumina APV, etc) with the 3800 would work too using the Fiero manual trans outer CV's. The automatic cv's are the wrong axle size.<P>Call CVUnlimited or some other CV/axle place and tell them you want 94 Trans Sport axle assemblies with manual transmission 86 Fiero outer CV's. Several places quoted about $80-90 for each side. The 4T60E/65E is the important part since the passenger side axle is slightly shorter than the 440/4T60 shaft.<P>Otherwise, hit the wrecking yards, find a 3800 U-van (all have 4T60E) or 3800/4T60E A-cars, get the complete axle assemblies and swap on the Fiero manual trans outer CV's/spindles.<P>The 4T65E is the same axle to axle width as the 4T60E.<BR> <BR>Hope that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowfunds||11-18-2000||01:02 PM||||Thanks for the info. Hey Terryk is the project you were working on up and running? How is everthing going?||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||11-18-2000||01:54 PM||||It's been running for about two weeks. Now. runs great. I have to go for recertification here pretty soon. I'm mainly doing cleanup now (wire routing, etc.) It's hard to select the best routing of hoses and wires until everything is in there, then it's easier to see what needs to be moved. The shift selector reverser seems to be working out well.<P>The DOHC swap might be running this weekend too.||||reg||14
